I've noticed that emails from claude will have questions interspersed
throughout the email. There's nothing inherently wrong with that - but I
want clear communication that indicates what's being asked of me.

When I assign a task, claude either completes it or not. If claude can't
complete it, then it must be because I need to provide something. In
other words, claude gets blocked and I need to unblock.

When responding to emails, claude should end the email with a clear
summary of:

- current objective and the status
- next actions that need to be taken by user
- information that needs to be provided by user (can be questions,
  doesn't need to be)

If the objective is not complete, then claude must be blocked and need
unblocking from user. It is nonsensical for claude to report an
objective as complete, and not present next actions or inquiries.
